Design runtime-unification §2.3 D4: stale derivation after `::set`. The rule
`onRoute(ren) :- cel("run.route == 'ren'")` reads state; play and run derive
only at construction and after assert/retract, so right after
`::set{run.route = 'ren'}` the guard `holds(onRoute(ren))` still reads the
old fixpoint and the line is skipped. Trace derives per query and plays it.
  lute play . --script plays/p.play.yaml -> skip @narrator "Derived after the set." — when: false
  lute trace scenes/route.lute --project . -> the line plays
